Z||000009||Fastback Formula||11-09-1999||11:49 PM||||I'm not sure if this works on UBB posts, but it's certainly worth a try...<P>60º &lt;- If that does in fact turn out to the degree symbol, you can follow the directions below to replicate it--<P>To find the different character codes in Windows 95/98/NT, open Character Map located in Start/Programs/Accessories, click on the character you would like, and then take note of the message in the bottom right corner of the window.  The message will be something like "keystroke: Alt+0186"  Type the key combination shown, and you're all set!<P>Later, Adam   :Þ||||reg||3
